//! WHY: Decision 031 — we own our WASM-format tooling. This module is a type-safe,
//! 1:1 model of the WebAssembly binary format: parse, edit, and re-serialize
//! `.wasm` with minimal diffs (`Lazy<T>` keeps untouched parts as raw bytes).
//!
//! WHAT: `Module` → sections → types/instructions/indices, with the codec and
//! visitor autogenerated by `foundation_macros::{Wasmbin, WasmbinCountable, Visit}`.
//!
//! HOW: Ported & adapted from `wasmbin` v0.9.2
//! (https://github.com/RReverser/wasmbin), © Google Inc. / Ingvar Stepanyan,
//! licensed Apache-2.0. Modifications for ewe_platform (Apache-2.0 §4(b)): lives as
//! a module of `foundation_codegen` (paths `crate::wasm::…`); derives come from
//! `foundation_macros`; `PathItem` and `DecodeError::in_path` are public so the
//! derives can expand outside this crate; WAT support is a planned extension
//! (feature 15). See `README.md` in this directory and the workspace `NOTICE`.

